<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain north, sun south.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain north, sun south.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Wednesday were forecast to see showers in the north, sun in the south, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see showers in the north with highs of 17 to 27 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see showers in the north, sun in the south with highs of 22 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 20 to 31 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
